WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.423
Week 22: Double Pronouns, Se, and Reference. report accidental events give concise instructions maintain reference across sentences

2
00:00:09.423 --> 00:00:23.649
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can report accidental events, give concise instructions, maintain reference across sentences. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:32.561
Language system. Double-object order; le/les to se; redundant indirect objects; accidental se; discourse reference.

4
00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:39.019
Sound and delivery. Pronoun clusters and accent restoration in affirmative commands.

5
00:00:39.019 --> 00:00:48.551
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:48.551 --> 00:01:14.937
Model language. Se me perdieron las llaves. — I lost my keys. El informe se lo mandé a Clara. — I sent the report to Clara. A ellos se les olvidó la cita. — They forgot the appointment. Explícaselo antes de la reunión. — Explain it to him or her before the meeting. No se nos cayó el equipo; falló el soporte. — We did not drop the equipment; the support failed.

7
00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:24.942
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
